## H2 — Grouped / nested heap vs sibling class
### Mechanism
| Rail | File | After wave-2 source | Concat? | In 07:49 ELF? |
|------|------|---------------------|---------|---------------|
| check / llvm / emit-c **front door** | `c_emit_secret.oo` L173–200 | Int `depth`; IDENT via `field_at` | **none** | **no** (still first-`)`) |
| `c_secret_scan_call` | same file L89–130 | same Int `depth` | **none** | **no** |
| stmt `println` emit | `c_emit_print.oo` L19–41 | Int `d`; IDENT still `"__sec__"+sn` | no ident rebuild; no join | **no** (still first-`)`) |
| free-call `eprintln` | `c_emit_lower.oo` L90 → `c_secret_emit_guard` | C-text `c_guard_scan_idents` (7.1 slice) | join is **`c_emit_call_args` L40** (pre-existing) | **yes** |

Wave-2 **source** check + stmt depth both **see `tok` after a nested `)`**. Host ELF still does **not**. On this binary, stmt println still stops at first `RPAREN` except when `tok` is a **later top-level arg** after `c_emit_expr_c` consumed the grouped first arg (`println((1), tok)` — 2nd-arg rescan). `println(("x") + tok)` stays one arg on this ELF: scan hits the grouping `RPAREN` and **never** looks at `tok`. WT stmt `d` would continue.

Host `oodac` is the **07:49** ELF (same as s61/s71/s72/s710/s28/s29). `nm -S` this binary (sizes unchanged):

| Sym | Addr | Size |
|-----|------|-----:|
| `c_emit_println` | `0x4651b0` | 2583 |
| `c_secret_emit_guard` | `0x461080` | 4738 |
| `c_guard_scan_idents` | `0x45fb90` | 5354 |
| `check_secret_println_sinks` | `0x475c50` | 5316 |
| `c_secret_scan_call` | `0x45e020` | 783 |
| `c_secret_refuse_println_ident` | `0x45de80` | 175 |

Live RSS below is **this ELF**, not the WT walker. Same honesty class as `s710_memory.oot` H2.

### Live rails (this binary)
Ephemeral `/tmp/s29b_mem_1171777/` (removed). `/usr/bin/time` `%e` / `%M`. `OODA_SRC_ROOT=ooda`. Isolated HOME (s71 R9). Taken **before** the 12:35 stmt `d` land; ELF unchanged so the table still holds.

Direct tiny fixtures:

| Case | cmd | rc | sec | RSS KB | Note |
|------|-----|---:|----:|-------:|------|
| `println(tok)` bare | emit-c | 1 | 0.07 | 4416 | `ERR secret println … tok` |
| same | check | 1 | 0.03 | 5108 | dual refuse |
| `println((1), tok)` grouped later | emit-c | 1 | 0.03 | 4792 | stmt 2nd-arg rescan; `oo_print_int((1LL));` then refuse |
| same | check | **0** | 0.03 | 5232 | **FN** — ELF has no depth |
| `eprintln((1), tok)` | emit-c | 1 | 0.04 | 4652 | guard |
| same | check | **0** | 0.02 | 5284 | same front-door miss |
| `println(("x") + tok)` | emit-c | **0** | 0.03 | 4920 | **FN leak** `oo_str_concat((oo_str_lit("x")), tok)` — ELF stmt no `d` |
| same | check | **0** | 0.03 | 5272 | FN |
| `eprintln(("x") + tok)` | emit-c | 1 | 0.03 | 4848 | guard still sees `tok` |
| same | check | **0** | 0.02 | 5328 | FN |
| public `println(1)` | emit-c | 0 | 0.02 | 4532 | no secret |

**Read:** grouped emit-c RSS **tracks** bare / eprintln (~4.4–4.8 MB). Check on the hole is the same 5.2 MB class as a public check (FN → typecheck, no refuse). **No** extra join buffer on the stmt rail. The eprintln save of concat-after-group is the **existing** 7.1 C-text scan, not a 2.9b alloc.

Harness `scripts/s29_println_guard_smoke.oo` (wave-2 rail added): wave-1 rails **OK**; `println((1), tok)` emit-c **OK** / check **FAIL**. Smoke **exit 1**. `s29b_harness.oot` names this. Do **not** treat exit 1 as a harness bug. Do **not** treat it as a memory FAIL.

Nested grouping `println( (^{d} 1 )^{d} , tok)` (stmt still refuses via 2nd-arg rescan; check FN so typechecks the nest):

| d | src B | emit-c sec / RSS | check sec / RSS |
|--:|------:|-----------------:|----------------:|
| 1 | 80 | 0.08 / 4732 | 0.03 / 5308 |
| 8 | 94 | 0.05 / 4728 | 0.07 / 5820 |
| 32 | 142 | 0.06 / 5988 | 0.06 / 7868 |
| 64 | 206 | 0.19 / 6712 | 0.11 / 10300 |
| 128 | 334 | 0.13 / 8880 | 0.25 / 15168 |
| 256 | 590 | 0.23 / 12984 | 0.38 / 24692 |

**Read:** RSS grows with **parse/typecheck of nested parens** (and with source bytes), **not** a prefix-chain. 64→128→256 check ≈ 1.47× / 1.63× RSS for 2× depth. A concat bomb on the walk would be tens–hundreds of MB at d=256. A rebuilt ELF that actually **runs** the Int depth walks pays `field_at` on the extra tokens the old walk skipped — O(#toks) slices, still **no** growing `args`.

Long SECRET ident after grouped first arg (`// SECRET: A+a*(N-1)` then `println((1), NAME)`):

| N | src B | emit-c sec / RSS (BLOCK) | check sec / RSS (FN on this ELF) |
|--:|------:|-------------------------:|---------------------------------:|
| 64 | 258 | 0.06 / 5816 | 0.03 / 5756 |
| 256 | 834 | 0.17 / 8696 | 0.12 / 6628 |
| 1024 | 3138 | 2.63 / 19696 | 0.61 / 11312 |
| 2048 | 6210 | 5.15 / 35028 | 1.83 / 16992 |

**Read:** time 1024→2048 ≈ 2.0–3.0× for 2× N — `char_at` / lex (same class as s29 H2 / s61 H2). emit-c RSS is the **ident token** + first-arg emit, then refuse — not a depth-walk concat. Check is cheaper here **because it FNs** (no secret walk of `NAME` on this ELF). Wave-1 bare-ident emit-c at N=2048 was 18.1 MB; this 35 MB includes the `let NAME = "s"` bind of a 2 KiB lexeme (`token_scan_ident` still per-char — **not** 2.9b).

Many public idents with a grouped dummy (`println|eprintln((1), a0000, …)`):

| N | src B | println emit sec / RSS / C B | eprintln emit sec / RSS / C B | println check | eprintln check |
|--:|------:|-----------------------------:|------------------------------:|--------------:|----------------:|
| 16 | ~458 | 0.08 / 7864 / 9912 | 0.09 / 8000 / 9636 | 0.13 / 11600 | 0.10 / 11556 |
| 64 | ~1754 | 0.64 / 26424 / 12264 | 0.72 / 26492 / 11220 | 0.52 / 46672 | 0.63 / 46408 |

**Read:** println **tracks eprintln** (same ~26 MB / ~46 MB class as s29 H2 N=64). Join on eprintln is still cheaper C text. Grouped dummy does **not** change the class.

**H2 heap class: PASS. H2 time: residual. H2 new-walk product-binary RSS: unproved (pre-depth host).**

