### Recipes (Memory OWN — hard; wave-2 addendum)
Wave-1 bar still stands. Wave-2 **landed the OK rows**:

| Recipe | Heap | Memory |
|--------|------|--------|
| **Int `depth` on the existing check token walk** | 0 delta | **PASS** (H1) |
| Same Int depth on `c_secret_scan_call` | 0 delta | **PASS** (reuse) |
| **Int `d` on stmt `c_emit_println` scan** (12:35) | 0 delta | **PASS** (reuse; no join) |
| **I3** check loop → `c_secret_scan_call(...)` | token fields; **0** concat | **OK** (would DRY the two Int walks) |
| Per-arg emit: `c_secret_emit_guard(env, "println", arg, "", "", arg)` after existing `c_emit_expr_c` | one slice-walk of **already-lowered** `arg` | **OK** (reuse; no join) |
| **I5** `joined = joined + ", " + arg` inside `c_emit_println` | **new** prefix-chain | **FAIL** |
| Keep per-arg `oo_print_*` **and** add a second join just to feed the guard | double lower + new concat | **FAIL** |
| **I9** check calls `c_secret_emit_guard` with fabricated `args` | new string rebuild or empty-args FN | **FAIL** |

`c_secret_emit_guard` still takes **C arg texts**, not toks. Depth is how you fix first-`)` **without** that signature lie.

Progress: every branch of the check / scan_call loops does `p = p + 1`. Stmt loop does `sp = p + 1` after the depth test. `depth` / `d` are scalars. No spin. No new string buffer.

**H3: PASS.**

